I’m happy to confirm that the coordinates you supplied—**37.4224764, –122.0842499**—are indeed correct. Those latitude/longitude values point to the Googleplex in Mountain View, California.

Below is a quick example of how you could retrieve that information using the Google Geocoding API (reverse‑geocoding). I’ll show the request you’d make and a typical JSON response you’d receive. (I can’t actually call the API from here, but this is what you’d see if you did.)

---

### 1️⃣ Request

```http
GET https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/geocode/json
    ?latlng=37.4224764,-122.0842499
    &key=YOUR_API_KEY
```

> **Note:** Replace `YOUR_API_KEY` with your actual Google Maps API key.

